{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Problem\n\nGraphQL costs 5,000 points per hour, account-wide, and the cost of `gh project` list commands scales with the **requested** `--limit`, not with what actually comes back. Measured against the demo project (8 items):\n\n| Call | Points |\n|---|---|\n| `gh project item-list --limit 500` (vig's `ITEM_LIMIT`) | **101** |\n| `gh project item-list --limit 50` | 51 |\n| `gh project field-list --limit 100` | **101** |\n| views query (#149), `issue list` / `pr list` (100), `repo view`, `issue view`, `pr view` | ~0 each |\n\nSo one board fetch costs **~200 points**, and a vig instance left on the Projects page (stale re-fetch every 5 minutes) burns **~2,400 points/hour** — two idle instances exhaust the whole account quota, taking `gh` and every other tool down with it (observed on 2026-09-07 with 11 forgotten instances).\n\n## Fix\n\n- `field-list --limit 30` (projects rarely have more; keep a re-fetch at 100 if 30 come back).\n- `item-list` starts at `--limit 100`; only when `totalCount` says the board is bigger, re-fetch once with the larger limit (up to the current 500). Boards ≤100 items — the common case — drop from ~200 to **~50 points** per fetch.\n- Piggy-back `rateLimit { used remaining }` on the views query (cost 0) and surface the remaining points in the status bar next to the existing `⚠ rate limited` indicator, so a burning quota is visible before it exhausts.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The REST `rate_limit` endpoint misreports the GraphQL resource (`used: 0` while the real `rateLimit.used` is 5000) — always read the GraphQL-side field.\n- Related: #135 added the backoff and `github-poll-interval`; this issue is about not spending the points in the first place.","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-07T07:25:24Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":163,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Projects: cut the GraphQL cost of a board fetch (limit-aware paging)"}
